      "writtenOn": "2024-10-10T18:43:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Bazel does handle transitive dependencies like that, however the best practice is to depend directly on the target that has the headers you need in `hdrs`. We have support built into our toolchain to check this, but it is opt-in. This is the `layering_check` feature you might have seen in some of the other `skia_cc_library` rules. I would expect if you added that to this target and tried to build, you would see errors about not depending on those targets directly.",
      "parentUuid": "f64bc163_1aab795a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 20
      },
