      "writtenOn": "2024-10-10T21:28:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Bazel does handle transitive dependencies like that, however the best practice is to depend directly on the target that has the headers you need in `hdrs`. We have support built into our toolchain to check this, but it is opt-in. This is the `layering_check` feature you might have seen in some of the other `skia_cc_library` rules. I would expect if you added that to this target and tried to build, you would see errors about not depending on those targets directly.\n\nNice!  Yes, I think I do want `layering_check`.  It does complain about missing dependencies as-is.  Let me fix this in the latest patchset.",
      "parentUuid": "4aeb7bf0_0c930671",
